{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אם בחקתי תלכו", :translit "im bechukotei telechu", :gloss "if in My statutes you walk"} {:he "עמלים בדברי תורה", :translit "ameilim bedivrei torah", :gloss "toiling in words of Torah"} {:he "סמך אם בחקותי לשבת", :translit "samach im bechukotai leshabbat", :gloss "it juxtaposed 'if in My statutes' to Sabbath"} {:he "ששקולים הם ככל המצות והחוקים", :translit "she-shakulim hem kechol hamitzvot vehachukim", :gloss "that they are equivalent to all the commandments and statutes"} {:he "ועוד סמך שבת לונתתי גשמיכם בעתם", :translit "ve'od samach shabbat levenatati gishmeichem be'ittam", :gloss "and further it juxtaposed Sabbath to 'I will give your rains in their season'"} {:he "דהיינו בלילי שבתות", :translit "hainu beleilei shabbatot", :gloss "that is, on Sabbath nights"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "אם בחקתי תלכו", :b "עמלים"}], :frame {:text "The Sifra interprets 'if you walk in My statutes' as meaning 'you shall toil in Torah' (ameilim ba-Torah), reading the verse not as mere obedience but as dedicated labor in Torah study (Sifra, Bechukotai 1:1–2). Shabbat is identified as equivalent to all the commandments: 'one who keeps it is as though he fulfilled them all' (Yerushalmi Nedarim 3:9 / Shemot Rabbah 25:12). Rain in its season (Lev 26:4) is understood as a specific reward, tied to Sabbath nights.", :sources ["Sifra Bechukotai 1:1–2" "Yerushalmi Nedarim 3:9" "Shemot Rabbah 25:12"]}} {:quotes [{:he "אם בחוקתי תלכו", :translit "im bechukotei telechu", :gloss "if in My statutes you walk"} {:he "אבת שתלכו בדרכי אבות", :translit "avot she-telechu bedarchei avot", :gloss "fathers, that you walk in the path of the fathers"} {:he "בחקתי תלכו", :translit "bechukotei telechu", :gloss "in My statutes you walk"} {:he "היא היראה", :translit "hi hayir'ah", :gloss "this is fear"} {:he "יראת י ה' היא אוצרו", :translit "yir'at Hashem hi otzro", :gloss "the fear of YHWH, it is His treasure"} {:he "אם תמלאו את אוצרותי אמלא אוצרותיכם", :translit "im temal'u et otzarotai emalei otzroteichem", :gloss "if you fill My treasuries, I will fill your treasuries"} {:he "יפתח ה' לך את אוצרו", :translit "yiftach Hashem lecha et otzro", :gloss "may YHWH open for you His treasure"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "אם בחקתי תלכו", :spells "אבת"}], :frame {:text "'The fear of YHWH, it is His treasure' quotes Isaiah 33:6. The phrase 'may YHWH open for you His treasure' quotes Deuteronomy 28:12. The Sifra identifies 'in My statutes you walk' with toil in Torah, which the Ba'al HaTurim further identifies as yir'ah, fear/awe of God (Sifra Bechukotai 1:1–2). Walking in the ways of the fathers evokes the patriarchal covenant of Genesis 18:19, 'that he may command his children after him to keep the way of YHWH.'", :sources ["Isaiah 33:6" "Deuteronomy 28:12" "Genesis 18:19" "Sifra Bechukotai 1:1–2"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ועשיתם אתם", :translit "va'asitem otam", :gloss "and you shall do them"} {:he "אותיות אמת", :translit "otiyot emet", :gloss "letters of truth"} {:he "א\"ן שתתעסקו בתורה", :translit "o she-tit'asku be-torah", :gloss "or that you engage in Torah"} {:he "דכתיב בה עשיה", :translit "she-katuv bah asi'ah", :gloss "for 'making' is written of it"} {:he "שכל טוב לכל עושיהם", :translit "vechol tov lechol oseihem", :gloss "every good to all who do them"} {:he "י' פסוקים מאם בחקותי (ר\"ל מן ונתתי) עד ואולך אתכם קוממיות", :translit "eser pesukim me-im bechukotai (omar: min venatati) ad va'olach etchem komemiyut", :gloss "ten verses from 'if in My statutes' (i.e., from 'I will give') until 'and I will lead you upright'"} {:he "כנגד עשרה ברכות שבויתן לך", :translit "keneged eser berachot shebayiten lach", :gloss "corresponding to ten blessings given therein to you"} {:he "וכנגד עשרת הדברות", :translit "ucheneged aseret hadibrot", :gloss "and corresponding to the Ten Commandments"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Rearrangement of letters of ועשיתם אתם yields אמת"} {:kind :other, :note "Wordplay linking עשיה (making) to עשיתם (you shall do) to Torah engagement via Psalms 119"} {:kind :masorah, :count 10, :occurrences []}], :frame {:text "Psalms 119:152 states 'all Your commandments are truth' (vechol mitzvotecha emet), linking commandments to emet, truth (Psalms 119:152). Psalms 111:10 says 'a good understanding to all who do them' (seichel tov lechol oseihem). Leviticus 26:3–13 contains a series of blessings; Deuteronomy 28:1–13 likewise contains blessings understood as ten-fold. The Ten Commandments appear at Exodus 20:2–14 and Deuteronomy 5:6–18.", :sources ["Psalms 119:152" "Psalms 111:10" "Leviticus 26:3–13" "Deuteronomy 28:1–13" "Exodus 20:2–14" "Deuteronomy 5:6–18"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "אם בחקתי תלכו", :a-value 1017, :b "עמלים", :b-value 190, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "אם בחקתי תלכו", :spells "אבת", :letters ["א" "ב" "ת"], :by :selah, :order :in-order} {:kind :other, :note "Rearrangement of letters of ועשיתם אתם yields אמת", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Wordplay linking עשיה (making) to עשיתם (you shall do) to Torah engagement via Psalms 119", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 10, :occurrences [], :by :selah, :located []}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:26:13.850989125Z", :model "glm-5.2"}